  abstract = {This chapter discusses a study to comapare the proliferative activity of lymphoid spleen cells and the antibody response in Rana esculenta kept at 22 and 4°C. Adult frogs kept at 22°C were immunized with 0.2 ml sheep red blood cells. On days 3, 6, 10, 13, 17, 22, 29, and 37 one dose of 3H thymidine was injected. After one hour, experimental animals were bled. Smears, prints, and histological sections were prepared from spleen, liver, bone marrow, and peripheral blood. Deep extra-and intrafollicular depletion of lymphocytes is found in spleens of both immunized and nonimmunized frogs in this temperature. Proliferation activity precedes the onset of antibody formation at least by 5–6 days in frogs kept at 22°C. The titer of hemagglutinins and hemolysins increased on day 17 and on day 29, it reached its maximum. No antibodies were detected in the sera of frogs kept at 4°C.},
